  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_balanced_dataloader(labels: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Balanced DataLoader** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_balanced_dataloader(labels: list) -> dict:\n    labs = np.array(labels, dtype=np.int64)\n    cl, cnt = np.unique(labs, return_counts=True)\n    cw = {int(c): round(float(len(labs)/(len(cl)*ct)), 4) for c, ct in zip(cl, cnt)}\n    return {'class_weights': cw, 'sample_weights': [round(cw[int(y)], 4) for y in labs]}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
